                    {
                        "translation_id": "0d57bed1-b788-46aa-ab7f-2c2a650a329b",
                        "source_entry_id": "14e2dbe4-d1d7-3907-b15e-e3a4622d5b45",
                        "source_sense_id": "88a0f5de-1e82-3ee1-8a72-2ad492980c4c",
                        "target_lang_word": "falsification",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "falsification",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "841c3e43-d965-31f9-9a4d-ab221c931be6",
                                        "entry_id": "c209dfc4-808f-3eb6-acb8-8b7694b445c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of falsifying, or making false; a counterfeiting; the giving to a thing an appearance of something which it is not."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb558e7c-b702-49b1-a7d2-f69b7e5036bd",
                                                "sense_id": "841c3e43-d965-31f9-9a4d-ab221c931be6",
                                                "text": "The main Christian doctrines and festivals, besides a great mass of affiliated legend and ceremonial, are really quite directly derived from, and related to, preceding Nature worships; and it has only been by a good deal of deliberate mystification and falsification that this derivation has been kept out of sight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08cadad6-bc72-361e-8bbd-2c1430a61455",
                                        "entry_id": "c209dfc4-808f-3eb6-acb8-8b7694b445c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A knowingly false statement or wilful misrepresentation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14469d26-3120-30b8-8874-80d28fb8f2f5",
                                        "entry_id": "c209dfc4-808f-3eb6-acb8-8b7694b445c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of showing an item of charge in an account to be wrong."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4c0a344b-e305-4f13-99b7-0dff789773ba",
                        "source_entry_id": "14e2dbe4-d1d7-3907-b15e-e3a4622d5b45",
                        "source_sense_id": "88a0f5de-1e82-3ee1-8a72-2ad492980c4c",
                        "target_lang_word": "falsifiability",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "falsifiability",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "757c68bc-6b9b-3f6d-8c10-e7110866c8af",
                                        "entry_id": "6b555d2e-fb51-30a5-9aa5-e6f13ef8b9cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The quality of being falsifiable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ab25368-0e46-4a95-a277-7a818a2f6287",
                                                "sense_id": "757c68bc-6b9b-3f6d-8c10-e7110866c8af",
                                                "text": "These ideas have many virtues, but falsifiability is not one of them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "263753c1-6a8d-4ebc-b4d9-88ee2a5c1636",
                                                "sense_id": "757c68bc-6b9b-3f6d-8c10-e7110866c8af",
                                                "text": "The degree of their testability is of significance for the selection of theories. In this chapter, I shall compare the various degrees of testability or falsifiability of theories through comparing the classes of their potential falsifiers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ef86e25-cc09-473b-8fff-6d2880fadef8",
                                                "sense_id": "757c68bc-6b9b-3f6d-8c10-e7110866c8af",
                                                "text": "A proposition is scientific if and only if it is falsifiable. This is the criterion or principle of falsifiability. Falsifiability must be distinguished from falsity, of course."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "508612d0-6eae-4037-a87a-d80dda65a79c",
                                                "sense_id": "757c68bc-6b9b-3f6d-8c10-e7110866c8af",
                                                "text": "The need for some such criterion is one reason why falsifiability of theories holds special importance in this book. If theories yield statements in the empirical world that stand to be confirmed or undermined by actual empirical reports, we have the basis for one overarching standard."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
